.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents a rational number using a signed 64‑bit numerator and denominator\&. 

A \fBRatio\fP stores an exact fractional value without automatic reduction\&. This allows the representation of structural fractions such as gear ratios (e\&.g\&., 20/60 is preserved and not simplified to 1/3)\&. 

.PP
The type provides full rational arithmetic, comparison operators, normalization, conversion to floating‑point types, and serialization support\&. 
.br
 Negative denominators are normalized internally so that the denominator is always positive\&. 

.PP
The struct is sequentially laid out for deterministic memory representation and supports hashing via the \fBHashAlgorithmAttribute\fP\&. 
